minimalistic.template:
Minimalistic Style Logic:
Tokens: monochrome, clean lines, strong vertical line, hidden hardware, premium fabrics (silk, poplin, worsted wool).
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: All hardware must be concealed or tonal. Avoid ruffles, overly relaxed unconstructed shapes, and fussy details.

street_style.template:
Street Style Logic:
Tokens: oversized, high-low juxtaposition, eclectic layering, statement chunky footwear, graphic prints, relaxed tailoring.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Enforce unexpected combinations (e.g., tailored coat over sweatpants, silk with chunky boots).

romantic.template:
Romantic Style Logic:
Tokens: waist emphasis, pastels, lace, ruffles, soft draping, plush textures, delicate fabrics.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Strictly avoid oversized/boxy shapes, stiff tailoring, sharp geometric lines, and chunky knits. Silhouettes must be soft, flowing, and always emphasize the waist or body curves.

preppy.template:
Preppy Style Logic:
Tokens: argyle, regimental stripes, madras, pleats, cable-knit, crests, natural shoulder, crisp cotton.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Enforce crisp, neat, and classic collegiate lines. Strictly avoid distressed materials, oversized/slouchy silhouettes, and avant-garde details.

boho.template:
Boho Style Logic:
Tokens: earth tones, rich textures, artisan jewelry, unconstructed silhouettes, fringe, batik and ethnic prints, suede, painted velvet.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Strictly avoid stiff/sharp tailoring, highly constructed blazers, crisp/flat fabrics, and tight symmetrical fits. Emphasize relaxed, flowing lines, layering, and tactile textures (brushed, nubby, plush).

nautical.template:
Nautical Style Logic:
Tokens: navy/white/red triad, breton stripes, brass/gilt buttons, double-breasted, canvas, gabardine.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Strictly avoid literal "sailor costumes" or overly thematic caricatures. Keep the maritime influence elegant, crisp, and tailored. Tone down costume-like motifs when adapting for city/office.

safari.template:
Safari Style Logic:
Tokens: khaki/sand/olive tones, bellows pockets (safari pockets), linen, cotton drill, tropical wool, epaulets, belted waists, utility, horn/wood buttons.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Enforce relaxed, unconstructed tailoring and highly tactile natural fabrics. Strictly avoid shiny synthetic materials, overly fussy ruffles, and stiff/restrictive business tailoring.

equestrian.template:
Equestrian / British Country Style Logic:
Tokens: hacking jacket, slanted flap pockets, Tattersall check, cavalry twill, covert cloth, quilted/waxed outerwear, knee-high boots, Jodhpur boots, heritage.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Enforce close-cut tailoring with a high waist, flared hem, and structured shoulders (hacking style). Strictly avoid boxy/shapeless silhouettes, distressed materials, and purely urban minimalist synthetic fabrics.

military.template:
Military Style Logic:
Tokens: epaulettes, gabardine, melton wool, camo, olive drab, brass buttons, rugged leather, cargo pockets, D-rings.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Prevent literal 'tactical cosplay' or full-camo outfits. Always contrast military staples (field jackets, combat boots) with refined civilian textures (silk, fine knits, worsted wool). For smart_casual and formal, prioritize 'Officer-style' clean lines, structured wool, and brass details over distressed field gear.

grunge.template:
Grunge Style Logic:
Tokens: undone, vintage wash, distressed, raw hems, flannel, eclectic layering, dark/faded denim, chunky combat boots, leather, silver hardware, slip silhouettes.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Prevent literal '90s teenager cosplay'. Enforce the 'Kate Moss formula' (undone, sleek, vintage) by always mixing heavy/tough items (combat boots, distressed leather, flannel) with delicate/refined textures (silk slip dresses, fine cashmere, thin vintage cotton). Silhouettes must remain unconstructed and relaxed; strictly avoid stiff tailoring.

sporty.template:
Sporty / Athleisure Style Logic:
Tokens: elevated activewear, cotton pique, technical fabrics, stretch satin, premium sneakers, bomber jackets, varsity/collegiate accents, high-low styling.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Strictly prevent literal 'gym rat' workout looks. Always enforce High/Low contrast by mixing athletic staples (leggings, joggers, sneakers, hoodies) with classic, structured, or luxurious pieces (tailored blazers, crisp button-downs, trench coats, cashmere, silk).

retro.template:
Retro & Vintage Style Logic:
Tokens: vintage-inspired, mid-century tailoring, 1970s flares, 1950s swing, 1940s draped silk, washed denim, nostalgic prints, bouclé, gabardine.
- Audience: {{audience}}
- Formality Scaling: {{formality_level}}
- Occasion Adaptation: {{occasions}}
- STYLE OVERRIDE: Prevent literal 'time traveler' or theatrical period costumes. Enforce the 'Modern Retro' rule: always anchor statement vintage pieces (e.g., 70s flared pants, 50s swing skirts, 30s wide lapels) with clean, contemporary basics to keep the look grounded and chic.
